Variables:
a, ta: first pair
b, tb: second pair
h, m: time (hours and minutes)
x = 60*h + m (start time in minutes from midnight?)
y = x + ta (end time? Actually y = x + ta)

z starts at 300 (which is 5:00 AM? 300 minutes = 5 hours). So z is a time variable starting at 300.

Then there is a loop (using goto jump) that increments z by b each iteration.

Conditions:
1. if (z + tb < x) -> then z = z + b; continue loop.
2. else if (z + tb > x && z < y && z < 1440) -> w++, z = z + b; continue loop.
3. else if (z > y) -> goto temp (exit loop)
4. else if (z + tb == x || z == y) -> z = z + b; continue loop.

Note: The conditions are checked in order. The loop continues until z > y (condition 3) or maybe other conditions lead to exit? Actually condition 3 is the only one that goes to temp. The others either continue loop or fall through? But note that after condition 4, it does z=z+b and goto jump. So the loop only exits when condition 3 is true (z > y). However, there is also a condition z < 1440 in condition 2. But if z >= 1440, condition 2 fails, then condition 3? If z > y, it exits. But what if z <= y but z >= 1440? Then condition 2 fails (because z<1440 false), condition 3: z>y? If z <= y, then condition 3 false. Condition 4: z+tb==x or z==y? Probably not. Then it would fall through to temp? Actually the code structure: after the else if chain, there is no explicit fallthrough; but in C, if none of the conditions match, it would just proceed to the next statement after the if-else chain. But here the if-else chain ends with the last else if, and then there is a label "temp:" after that. So if none of the conditions are true, it would just go to the next line which is "temp:" and print w. So the loop exits when z > y (condition 3) OR when none of the conditions match (which would be when z <= y but condition 2 fails because z>=1440, and condition 4 fails). But condition 2 has z<1440, so if z>=1440 and z<=y, then condition 2 false, condition 3 false (since z<=y), condition 4 likely false, so it falls through to temp. So effectively the loop runs while z <= y and z < 1440? But condition 1 and 4 also continue the loop.

